I am getting errors following the examples from D&R Examples <http://tessera.io/docs-datadr/#dr-examples> of Tessera web page.

Specifically at this step where there is a comment:
# divide by edGroup and filter out "Preschool"

The web page, I presume is auto-generated, because it is listing errors as well; but my error is different. When issuing:

byEdGroup <- divide(adultDdfGroup, by = "edGroup",
   filterFn = function(x) x$edGroup[1] != "Preschool",
   update = TRUE)

The error I get is:

* Verifying parameters...
* Applying division...
Error in if (kvApply(filterFn, list(reduce.key, res))) { :
  argument is of length zero

I am on R 3.1.2. Mac OS X. Issuing traceback():

6: eval(expr, envir, enclos)
5: eval(reduce$post, envir = reduceEnv)
4: mrExecInternal.kvMemoryList(data, setup = setup, map = map, reduce = reduce,
       output = output, control = control, params = params)
3: mrExecInternal(data, setup = setup, map = map, reduce = reduce,
       output = output, control = control, params = params)
2: mrExec(data, setup = setup, map = map, reduce = reduce, output = output,
       overwrite = overwrite, control = control, params = c(params,
           parList), packages = packages)
1: divide(adultDdfGroup, by = "edGroup", filterFn = function(x) x$edGroup[1] !=
       "Preschool", update = TRUE)

Could it be something to do with missing braces/curly brackets in the function?

Thanks in advance.

